<!--
  datamodel="sce-static" (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15): a `<param>` of a
  `<send>` or `<invoke>` the HOST serves carries the value of a typed
  expression, read from the machine's own fields at the moment the send or the
  invoke happens.

  Until it was lowered, a `<param expr>` here was typed, accepted and then
  never evaluated against the fields: the Kotlin machine sent an empty payload,
  the Rust machine called a script engine it had not been given and did not
  compile, and a host invoke read a copy of the variable inside a script engine
  that `<assign>` never wrote. Which of the four happened was the backend's, and
  none of them was the value the document wrote.

  The run `bump`, `go` changes `count`, `ready` and `label` before the send and
  the invoke read them, so a copy taken at start-up (`count` 3, `ready` false,
  `label` "idle") is told from the value the fields hold now (`count` 4,
  `ready` true, `label` "busy"):

    send    count = 4   ready = true   label = "busy"   twice = 8
            delta = -5  ratio = 1.5
    invoke  the same

  `twice` is an expression rather than a variable, so a lowering that handled
  only a bare name would still be wrong here. `delta` (a signed 16-bit
  integer) and `ratio` (a real) are the other kinds of value a param carries:
  a negative number and a fraction cross as the text and the JSON number they
  spell. `boom` is `count * 2000000000`, which a 32-bit field cannot hold: the
  checked multiplication fails, so its pair is left out and `error.execution` is
  raised (W3C SCXML 5.7.1) while the message still goes and the invocation
  still starts. `errors` counts those, one for the send and one for the invoke,
  so a lowering that dropped the pair without saying so is told from one that
  reported it.

  Four more sends carry one value as their `<content expr>` instead of pairs
  (SCE Accepted Subset §2.15): that value is the event's whole data, as JSON,
  and what the host is handed as the request's `content`, as text. `value` is
  `count * 2` (the number 8, as `8` both ways), `text` is `label` (the string
  "busy", as `"busy"` in the data and `busy` as the content), and `lost` is
  `count * 2000000000`, which the field cannot hold: the content is then the
  empty string, as W3C SCXML 5.6.2 has it, so the request carries `""` as its
  data and no content, `error.execution` is raised, and the message still goes.
  `errors` counts that report too, so it is three: the pairs' `boom`, this and
  the invoke's. A send that raises an error ends the block it is in (W3C SCXML
  4.9), so each of the two that fail in the run `bump`, `go` has an `<onentry>`
  of its own, and the four requests go out in document order: the pairs,
  `value`, `text`, `lost`. `after` follows `lost` in its block and is never
  sent, which is how the end of the block is told from a block that goes on.

  The invoke names `delta` and `ratio` in its `namelist` where the send writes
  them as params: a `namelist` name is the `<param name="x" expr="x"/>` it
  abbreviates, so the host is handed the same pairs either way, and the one
  set of assertions every backend makes about the request holds for both.

  The invoke's `src` is computed too (`srcexpr`, a string the machine holds,
  chosen by a condition that multiplies a field, so the expression can fail).
  `big` makes `count` too large for that multiplication, and an invocation whose
  source cannot be computed starts nothing: the host is never asked, which the
  start log says.

  The invoke's `content` — the body the service runs — is computed the same way
  (`<content expr>`, a string: `label`, chosen by a condition that multiplies a
  field of its own, `huge`, so it can fail on its own). `bloat` makes `huge` too
  large for that multiplication while `count` stays as it is, so an invocation
  whose body cannot be computed starts nothing though its source could be, and a
  source that failed first is told from a body that did.

  Deliberately single-axis: no event payload, no delay. The send's `namelist`
  is held by `static_send_namelist`. `statechart_host_processor.scxml` owns the
  dispatch under `ecmascript`; this one owns what a typed expression puts on
  the wire.

  Generated with BOTH host declarations, processor and invoker, naming the type
  x-sce-host (scripts/regen_host_processor.sh and
  scripts/regen_host_processor_kotlin.sh name the flags; an XML comment cannot
  spell a double hyphen).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0" initial="idle" datamodel="sce-static"
       name="statechart_static_host_params">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="count" sce:type="uint32" expr="3"/>
    <data id="ready" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="label" sce:type="string" sce:capacity="16" expr="'idle'"/>
    <data id="delta" sce:type="int16" expr="-5"/>
    <data id="ratio" sce:type="float64" expr="1.5"/>
    <data id="tag" sce:type="string" sce:capacity="16" expr="'job://params'"/>
    <data id="huge" sce:type="uint32" expr="1"/>
    <data id="errors" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
  </datamodel>

  <state id="idle">
    <transition event="bump">
      <assign location="count" expr="count + 1"/>
      <assign location="ready" expr="true"/>
      <assign location="label" expr="'busy'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="big">
      <assign location="count" expr="3000000000"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bloat">
      <assign location="huge" expr="3000000000"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="go" target="working"/>
  </state>

  <state id="working">
    <onentry>
      <send type="x-sce-host" target="somewhere" event="notify">
        <param name="count" expr="count"/>
        <param name="ready" expr="ready"/>
        <param name="label" expr="label"/>
        <param name="twice" expr="count * 2"/>
        <param name="delta" expr="delta"/>
        <param name="ratio" expr="ratio"/>
        <param name="boom" expr="count * 2000000000"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <onentry>
      <send type="x-sce-host" target="somewhere" event="value">
        <content expr="count * 2"/>
      </send>
      <send type="x-sce-host" target="somewhere" event="text">
        <content expr="label"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <onentry>
      <send type="x-sce-host" target="somewhere" event="lost">
        <content expr="count * 2000000000"/>
      </send>
      <send type="x-sce-host" target="somewhere" event="after">
        <content expr="count"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <invoke type="x-sce-host" id="h" namelist="delta ratio"
            srcexpr="count * 2 &gt; 0 ? tag : tag">
      <content expr="huge * 2 &gt; 0 ? label : label"/>
      <param name="count" expr="count"/>
      <param name="ready" expr="ready"/>
      <param name="label" expr="label"/>
      <param name="twice" expr="count * 2"/>
      <param name="boom" expr="count * 2000000000"/>
    </invoke>
    <transition event="error.execution">
      <assign location="errors" expr="errors + 1"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke.h" target="done"/>
  </state>

  <final id="done"/>
</scxml>
